    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d822">

                <pb facs="1012" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.014/12–2647</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Air Force</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Symington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-26">December 26, 1947</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Reference is made to your
                    letter of 11 December 1947 (CA 893.014/11–2147)<anchor n="9" xml:id="d822-f1"/>
                    concerning proposals made by the Chinese Government for the aerial mapping of
                    certain Chinese Provinces.</p>
                <p>Please be advised that the letter of 21 November from the Department <pb
                        facs="1013" n="1003" xml:id="pg1003"/> of the Army had previously been
                    coordinated with and does express the views of the Department of the Air
                    Force.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart Symington</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
